The 2020 moderation framework stated that adults of legal drinking age could choose not to drink or limit intake to 1 drink or less per day for women and 2 drinks or less per day for men, noting that some adults, such as pregnant women, should not drink [v4fresh-cand-pair-v4-new-052-old]. The 2025–2030 advice expands the groups who should completely avoid alcohol to include:
* pregnant women [v4fresh-cand-pair-v4-new-052-new];
* people recovering from alcohol use disorder or those unable to control the amount they drink [v4fresh-cand-pair-v4-new-052-new];
* people with medical conditions or taking medications that can interact with alcohol [v4fresh-cand-pair-v4-new-052-new].

Additionally, the 2025–2030 advice specifies that individuals with a family history of alcoholism should be mindful of associated addictive behaviors and alcohol consumption [v4fresh-cand-pair-v4-new-052-new].
